    "create_time": 1788406365.288,
    "update_time": 1788406369.7564359,
    "content": {
     "content_type": "text",
     "parts": [
      "Yes, driving is driving, whether or not you own the car. If you're a CA resident and you drive (including car-share or rentals), you're expected to hold a California license after the 10-day window. Zipcar's own eligibility checks may also start asking for a license matching your address when you update your profile. Book the DMV appointment. Wait times in SF can be a few weeks out."
     ]
    },
